#: includes/abilities.php:498
msgid "Get animation effects"
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:499
msgid "Lists the animation modes and every effect (what it looks like, where it can be used, its directions and options), the easings, the JSON Schema of an animation recipe, and examples. Read this first."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:515
msgid "Get a post's animations"
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:516
msgid "Lists every block of a post, page, template or pattern with its path, type, a text excerpt, whether it can be animated, and its animation as a recipe (null when it has none). Use the paths with set-animations."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:534
msgid "Validate an animation recipe"
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:535
msgid "Checks a recipe without changing anything. Returns each problem with its path and a fix hint, and the block attributes it would write. Pass block_name for the block-specific rules (image-only effects, stagger)."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:563
msgid "Set animations on a post"
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:564
msgid "Sets or removes the animation of one or more blocks of a post, page, template or pattern, and saves it straight away (also when published). All changes are validated first; if any is invalid nothing is saved and every problem is reported. The save stores a revision, so it can be rolled back. Each change names the block_name get-animations reported at that path, to guard against the content having changed since. Refused while another user has the post open in the editor."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:611
msgid "List saved animations"
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:612
msgid "Lists the site's saved animation library and the animations the theme ships, each as a recipe ready for set-animations. Needs a user who can manage site settings, like the library in the editor."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:631
msgid "Save an animation to the library"
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:632
msgid "Adds a recipe to the site's saved animation library under a name, so editors can apply it from the Motion Effects panel. Needs a user who can manage site settings."
msgstr ""

